But also, I'm not saying that, in five years, Optimus Prime is gonna land on Earth and start ripping Decepticon heads off.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:52.240
I'm saying that the technology we have today makes Transformers closer to fact than they are to fiction.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:56.240
ESPECIALLY when you look at what these automotive behemoths are really made out of.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.240
Which nicely segues to the question,

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.360
what are they actually made out of?

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:04.100
Well, it turns out the source material says a lot of different things.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.280
The Transformers have no less than four separate origin stories.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.460
Whether you're talking about the OG Marvel comics, the original tv show,

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:12.660
the UK version,

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:13.920
or the live-action movies,

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.440
this franchise is exhausting!

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.720
And don't even get me started on the Beast Wars!

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.080
Man, I love that show!

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.280
To me, Megatron will always be

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.760
a cute purple T-Rex

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.660
So if conflicting stories wasn't bad enough

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:26.580
then they all use words like:

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:27.820
"QUINTESSON"

